  "reason": "All 7 completed experiments used multiprofile, so the profile-setting dimension is entirely unexplored. The top performer (config_001: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) achieved 0.725 accuracy. Config_050 is the exact singleprofile counterpart of config_001 (same scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion; aggregation is None since singleprofile has no multi-profile aggregation step). This directly tests whether collapsing to a single profile changes performance meaningfully. If singleprofile matches or exceeds 0.725, it reveals a new promising axis; if it falls short, it confirms multiprofile is essential and the remaining 2 experiments should focus on fine-tuning within the multiprofile space (e.g., exploring scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted in config_022, which pairs the higher-F1 image encoder with a different aggregation). This is the highest-information experiment available: it resolves a binary design question with the strongest known parameter combination, making the best use of the limited remaining budget."
}

